<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar production slows as season nears end.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar production slows as season nears end.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai sugar crush progressed much more slowly this week as more than half the local mills have closed operations for the season, industry sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The season might end sooner than anticipated due to lower-than-expected sugar cane output. A total of 29 of 46 mills have closed so far, they told Reuters.</p>
<p>The crushing season normally starts in November and ends in May or June.</p>
<p>As of April 17, sugar production reached 5.75 million tonnes compared with 5.81 million tonnes in the corresponding period last year.</p>
<p>Comparison of this season's sugar cane crushing details with the same period last season (in tonnes unless specified):</p>
<p>				 April 17, 1997    April 17, 1996</p>
<p> Crushed sugar		   55,844,665	   55,121,801</p>
<p> Raw sugar			  3,086,662	    3,269,821</p>
<p> White sugar			2,669,658	    2,545,915</p>
<p> Yield (kg/tonne)		    103.08		 105.51</p>
<p> Commercial Cane Sugar (pct)	11.09		  12.04</p>
<p> Molasses			   2,519,225	    2,654,183</p>
<p> Yield				    45.11		  48.15</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
